@startuml
title NOTIFY — In-App Notification Center

skinparam dpi 300
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam ArrowColor #64748B
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #CBD5E1
skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
skinparam ActorBorderColor #3B82F6
skinparam ActorBackgroundColor #EFF6FF
skinparam DatabaseBorderColor #94A3B8
skinparam DatabaseBackgroundColor #F8FAFC

hide footbox
autonumber

actor "Authenticated User" as User
boundary "Notification Center UI" as UI
control "Spring Security" as Security
control "TenantWebInterceptor" as Interceptor
boundary "NotificationController" as Controller
control "NotificationService" as Service
database "Tenant DB (MySQL)" as TenantDB

note over User, Security
  Preconditions: tenant ACTIVE; JWT belongs to this tenant;
  inbox rows already exist for the caller (written by the dispatcher).
  This function does not send WebSocket or email.
end note

== Open inbox ==

User -> UI: Open notification center
activate UI
UI -> Security: GET /api/v1/notifications
activate Security

alt Unauthenticated or forbidden
  Security --> UI: 401 Unauthorized / 403 Forbidden
  deactivate Security
  UI --> User: Show access error
else Authorized
  Security -> Interceptor: Forward authenticated request
  activate Interceptor
  deactivate Security
  Interceptor -> Interceptor: setCurrentTenant(tenantId)
  Interceptor -> Controller: Route request
  activate Controller
  Controller -> Service: listMine(actorId, unreadOnly)
  activate Service
  Service -> TenantDB: Load caller's notifications and unread count
  activate TenantDB
  TenantDB --> Service: Items + unreadCount
  deactivate TenantDB
  Service --> Controller: NotificationListResponse
  deactivate Service
  Controller --> UI: 200 OK
  deactivate Controller
  UI --> User: Render list and unread badge
  Interceptor -> Interceptor: clear TenantContext
  deactivate Interceptor
end

== Mark read ==

User -> UI: Mark one or mark all as read
UI -> Security: PATCH mark-read (one or all)
activate Security

alt Unauthenticated or forbidden
  Security --> UI: 401 Unauthorized / 403 Forbidden
  deactivate Security
  UI --> User: Show access error
else Authorized
  Security -> Interceptor: Forward authenticated request
  activate Interceptor
  deactivate Security
  Interceptor -> Interceptor: setCurrentTenant(tenantId)
  Interceptor -> Controller: Route request
  activate Controller

  alt Mark one notification
    Controller -> Service: markRead(actorId, id)
    activate Service
    Service -> TenantDB: Find by id AND user_id
    activate TenantDB
    TenantDB --> Service: Row or empty
    deactivate TenantDB
    alt Missing or not owned by caller
      Service --> Controller: 404 Not Found
      deactivate Service
      Controller --> UI: 404
      UI --> User: Keep unread state
    else Found
      Service -> TenantDB: SET read_at = now() if still null
      activate TenantDB
      TenantDB --> Service: Updated
      deactivate TenantDB
      Service --> Controller: NotificationResponse
      deactivate Service
    end
  else Mark all
    Controller -> Service: markAllRead(actorId)
    activate Service
    Service -> TenantDB: SET read_at = now() WHERE user_id AND read_at IS NULL
    activate TenantDB
    TenantDB --> Service: Updated row count
    deactivate TenantDB
    Service --> Controller: MarkAllReadResponse
    deactivate Service
  end

  Controller --> UI: 200 OK
  deactivate Controller
  UI --> User: Unread badge decreases
  Interceptor -> Interceptor: clear TenantContext
  deactivate Interceptor
end

deactivate UI

note over UI, TenantDB
  Deep-link click only navigates inside the current tenant using payload_json.
  Resource screens belong to Job, Pipeline, Assessment, or Interview.
end note

@enduml
